echo x - net/titian/pkg-descr
sed 's/^X//' >net/titian/pkg-descr << '9a00c7cccdea11b8b5149284ea73031c'
XTitian is a Cisco/Junos-style command-line interface for FreeBSD
Xrouters, built on klish 2.2.5 with BIRD underneath. It provides
Xinterface, routing, BGP, OSPF, firewall/NAT, checkpoint/rollback
Xand startup-config replay through a single hierarchical CLI.
X
XThis port installs the klish runtime under /opt/titian together
Xwith the Titian XML command tree, the helper scripts, the BIRD
Xsection templates, the titian wrapper and the titian rc script.
XBIRD itself is a run-time dependency (net/bird2) and stays
Xdisabled by default; it is enabled from inside the CLI, never
Xby the installer.
9a00c7cccdea11b8b5149284ea73031c
echo x - net/titian/pkg-message
sed 's/^X//' >net/titian/pkg-message << '6afc2c03d0a18100538241301b2b4ca5'
XTo enable titian at boot:
X
X  sysrc titian_enable="YES"
X  service titian start
X
XBIRD stays disabled by default (bird_enable="NO"). Do NOT add
Xbird_enable="YES" to rc.conf by hand: enable BIRD from inside
Xthe Titian CLI instead, where the FRR/BIRD mutual-exclusion
Xcheck runs. The port never writes bird.conf and never touches
Xrc.conf.
6afc2c03d0a18100538241301b2b4ca5
